WEBVTT

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:18.370
I almost went back to sleep!

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:20.870
I need to go to school early and mount paper!

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:23.760
I gotta pull myself together...

00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:26.260
and start my day!

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:45.220
youki ni kuchibue fuite

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:45.220
Whistling a cheerful tune

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:47.560
madobe no kotori to sesshon

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:47.560
I join the birds chirping by the window

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:50.480
suima ga yatte kite

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:50.480
When fatigue strikes

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:53.100
atama ga danshingu

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:53.100
My imagination runs wild

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.560
nan demo kan demo waraeru nichijou

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.560
Everything in life makes me smile

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:58.400
okimari na kishoutenketsu

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:58.400
Nothing really new takes place

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:01.030
demo demo tama ni wa piritto supaisu

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:01.030
But sometimes it's exciting to spice things up

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:03.660
aozora peintingu

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:03.660
Let's paint it on the blue sky

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:04.700
doko ikou

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:04.700
Where should we go?

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:06.280
koko ni iyou

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:06.280
Let's stay here

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:07.280
sore wa nani

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:07.280
What's that?

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:08.870
are yaritai

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:08.870
I wanna try that!

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:11.460
ima ni tokubetsu na shirushi

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:11.460
Let's make this moment count

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.840
tokeibari no mawashikata watashi shidai kamo

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.840
How fast my clock moves is all up to me

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:20.510
shiki oriori iro toridori

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:20.510
With a rich palette of colors from the four seasons

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:22.970
nonbiri na everyday

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:22.970
Our laid-back everyday lives can be

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:25.590
pasuteru bibiddo metoro

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:25.590
Any blend of pastel, vivid, and metro colors

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:28.430
jibun dake no karaaringu

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:28.430
Anyone can create their own coloring

00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:31.020
sono tokidoki mune doki doki

00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:31.020
So when your heart races in excitement

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:34.730
hachamecha na taiyou ni oegaki

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:34.730
Just draw a sun at the top

00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:38.860
tobidasu aatishizumu

00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:38.860
And let your inner artist take you from there

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:42.190
gyutto shite ii kana

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:42.190
Can I hold your hand tight?

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:49.580
suki suki suki wo sukecchi

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:49.580
I've been sketching everything I love

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:52.120
nijiiro ni somete iku yo

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:52.120
And painting them in rainbow colors

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:56.800
sore ja ittekimasu

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:56.800
All right, I'm off to have some more fun!

00:01:57.010 --> 00:02:02.010
October 5th-6th,

00:01:57.010 --> 00:02:02.010
Pamphlet Compepe

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:10.150
All right!

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:12.060
And the paper's mounted!

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:15.680
I wonder what today's subject is.

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:16.360
Huh?

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:18.890
Whatcha doing, Yunocchi?

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:21.740
Just making a little good-luck charm.

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:24.330
I hope I can make a wonderful piece of art.

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:27.810
Oh yeah, you don't turn in the taped part, after all.

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:29.030
How neat!

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:29.710
Really?

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:32.090
Yeah, I think that's a great idea!

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:39.630
Yuno-san, your paper-mounting tape is frightening!

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:45.850
Everyone, please take a look at the handout!

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:49.810
Now I'll explain today's assignment for two-dimensional art class.

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:54.400
"Draw the cover of a pamphlet to be passed out at the Yamabuki Festival this year."

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:57.570
"A3 size, vertical orientation, you may use any materials you like."

00:02:57.570 --> 00:02:59.200
"One will be selected"?

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:00.550
It's a competition?

00:03:00.550 --> 00:03:02.110
Wow!

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:05.570
If they put it on the cover, then people from outside the school will get to see it too, won't they?

00:03:05.570 --> 00:03:07.330
Oh no, that's an understatement.

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:10.710
I'm sure they'll post it on the Yamabuki High website,

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:13.210
where the entire world can see it!

00:03:13.330 --> 00:03:15.340
It'd be a world debut!

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:17.590
Hello, Mom?

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:21.340
Um, I might be making a world debut.

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:22.790
A world debut?

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:24.390
What are you talking about?

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:29.140
Uh... never mind. It's actually pretty unlikely.

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:34.290
Yunocchi, what medium are you gonna use?

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:36.570
Um... Acrylic paint, I guess.

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:39.400
I see. I wonder what I should pick, then.

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:41.550
Yamabuki Festival...

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:44.450
What's our class doing this year?

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:46.750
Oh yeah, we haven't decided yet.

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:47.990
Maybe we'll put on a play again.

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:48.950
Maybe an exhibition?

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:50.730
We should do a costume party.

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:53.250
I want to do a costume party.

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:55.110
Don't you love costume parties?

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:59.250
<i>Yamabuki Festival, Yamabuki Festival...</i>

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:01.730
<i>Last year, we drew pictures and performed a play.</i>

00:04:01.730 --> 00:04:03.550
<i>Some people even recorded it.</i>

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:05.720
<i>There was a takoyaki stand too.</i>

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:07.720
<i>It was so lively.</i>

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:10.970
<i>Turning all those memories into a picture sounds fun.</i>

00:04:10.970 --> 00:04:12.730
<i>Like being in charge of lighting for the play...</i>

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:14.560
<i>Or the Principal's statue...</i>

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:16.560
<i>Let's not put that one.</i>

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:20.990
Huh?

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:22.590
Where did it go?

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:23.990
Miya-chan, what's wrong?

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:27.570
Yunocchi, can I borrow your rolling pin?

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:29.030
I can't find mine.

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:30.200
Rolling pin?

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:31.200
What do you mean?

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:34.080
You know, a <i>rolling</i> pin.

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:34.960
Oh!

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:37.460
Do you mean a ruling pen?

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:38.590
What? Ruling?

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:41.550
That's how it's pronounced?!

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:44.130
I used to make mistakes like that too.

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:45.760
I'm sure it happens to all the art students.

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:47.550
No, just you two.

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:54.490
It's lunchtime!

00:04:54.490 --> 00:04:56.910
Do you want to buy some bread and just eat it here?

00:04:56.910 --> 00:04:59.980
Sure. I was thinking the same thing, actually.

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:01.940
Huh?

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:03.320
Hiro-san!

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:05.820
Oh, Yuno-san, Miya-chan!

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:07.290
Getting bread today?

00:05:07.290 --> 00:05:10.750
Yeah, since we're working on something in the art classroom.

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:12.130
Are you getting bread too?

00:05:12.130 --> 00:05:15.410
Yeah. But there are many different kinds, so it's hard to pick one.

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:17.870
What's your in-class assignment for today?

00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:19.370
We have a drawing session.

00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:23.250
We're drawing a potential cover for the Yamabuki Festival pamphlet.

00:05:23.250 --> 00:05:25.730
And only one will be chosen! It's a competition!

00:05:25.730 --> 00:05:27.350
Wow, that brings back memories!

00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:29.910
I remember doing that last year.

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:32.630
They're only going to pick one, so it's not easy.

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:34.250
I'm trying pretty hard!

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:35.710
See you later, then.

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:36.850
See you!

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:39.940
Nazuna!

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:41.730
Nori-chan!

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:43.070
What are you getting today?

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:45.890
I haven't decided yet.

00:05:45.890 --> 00:05:48.230
You should decide before it's your turn.

00:05:48.230 --> 00:05:48.990
Yeah...

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:50.250
How about you, Nori-chan?

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:51.910
I'm getting Meal B.

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:55.950
I wish I could be as decisive as you.

00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:58.330
You just have to choose what you want to eat!

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:00.450
There's not much to worry about.

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:02.170
Yeah, but...

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:06.510
Sometimes I think the meal voucher system is a waste.

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:11.300
You need a huge machine that needs to be running all the time.

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:15.230
It'd be quicker and easier to just tell our orders directly to the dining staff,

00:06:15.230 --> 00:06:17.390
and it'd mean less time lining up, wouldn't it?

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:19.520
Well, I guess so.

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:23.060
But I think I'm more comfortable using meal vouchers.

00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:26.710
I'm a quiet person, so I'd get more nervous otherwise.

00:06:26.710 --> 00:06:29.780
Lining up gives me time to decide what to get.

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:33.270
Oh, I didn't think about it like that.

00:06:33.270 --> 00:06:35.020
That's so like you.

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:37.990
Is it? You think so?

00:06:37.990 --> 00:06:39.420
It's just who you are.

00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:40.970
Have you decided yet?

00:06:40.970 --> 00:06:42.230
You're up next.

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:43.770
Um...

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:44.750
Then...

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:46.550
Meal B.

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:52.300
Okay, 45 minutes remaining!

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:54.810
Start wrapping up!

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:58.020
<i>Oh, only 45 minutes left.</i>

00:06:58.020 --> 00:07:00.390
<i>There are still spots I haven't painted,</i>

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:03.110
<i>and I was gonna add the "Yamabuki Festival" text too.</i>

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:06.400
<i>I should skip the text.</i>

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:12.010
<i>I didn't have time to finish up my piece for the
personal exhibition at last year's Yamabuki Festival.</i>

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:15.700
<i>I can still make it if I hurry!</i>

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:18.790
<i>I don't want to turn in unfinished work!</i>

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:26.210
All right, time's up!

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:29.210
I made it!

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:32.310
Yunnochi, I like it! It's cute!

00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:34.230
You think so? Thanks.

00:07:34.230 --> 00:07:36.350
How did yours turn out?

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:39.570
Wow, that's very bold!

00:07:39.570 --> 00:07:41.090
I can feel the excitement.

00:07:41.090 --> 00:07:42.980
There's more to it.

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:44.670
It pops out if you wear these!

00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:46.230
3D?!

00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:53.990
And once again we have all these masterpieces.

00:07:53.990 --> 00:08:00.250
It's such a joy being able to see fresh, perceptive artwork every year.

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:02.670
Indeed! Even judging them gives me the chills.

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:06.530
Ikezawa-sensei, there are so many good ones!

00:08:06.530 --> 00:08:08.230
It's so hard to decide!

00:08:08.230 --> 00:08:10.920
What do you want me to do? Please don't hang on to me like that.

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:13.770
How do you feel about these?

00:08:13.770 --> 00:08:14.260
Well...

00:08:14.740 --> 00:08:17.490
There are a lot of fun pieces. I like it.

00:08:17.490 --> 00:08:18.260
Yeah!

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:22.270
There are a lot of well-done pieces this year, so it should be worthwhile.

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:23.270
Yep!

00:08:23.270 --> 00:08:25.130
How do you feel about them, Yoshinoya-sensei?

00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:30.190
Well, we should pick one that
really illustrates the excitement of the festival!

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:31.070
Good point!

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:37.910
What do you think about this piece?

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:40.570
Good morning!

00:08:40.570 --> 00:08:41.580
Morning!

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:43.590
Yuno-san, look at this.

00:08:43.590 --> 00:08:44.770
You did it!

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:48.670
What?

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:55.430
Yunocchi, that's amazing!

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:57.050
Congrats!

00:08:57.050 --> 00:08:58.180
Great job!

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:00.510
Me...

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:06.470
Yuno, congratulations on your piece getting chosen.

00:09:06.470 --> 00:09:08.030
Congratulations!

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:09.270
You did it!

00:09:09.270 --> 00:09:10.930
Thanks, everyone.

00:09:10.930 --> 00:09:12.480
Yuno-san, great job.

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:16.590
It's so amazing that your piece is going to be the cover!

00:09:16.590 --> 00:09:18.240
You're the only one in the entire school!

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:23.280
Then go ahead and give us a winner's speech.

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:24.790
Come on!

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:29.330
I am very happy!

00:09:29.330 --> 00:09:30.290
Bravo!

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:31.300
Why English?!

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:36.750
Yuno-san, who do you want to talk to about this right now?

00:09:36.750 --> 00:09:39.050
Huh? Oh, I should make a phone call!

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:45.560
Oh, Mom?

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:49.130
It's about what I mentioned yesterday.

00:09:49.130 --> 00:09:52.350
Yeah, that's how it turned out. Thanks.

00:09:52.350 --> 00:09:53.750
Yeah... yeah.

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:56.820
Okay. See you, then.

00:09:56.820 --> 00:09:58.250
And that's the story.

00:09:58.250 --> 00:10:00.620
A world debut, huh?

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:03.910
I should make her move to an apartment with high security!

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:06.790
And hire two bodyguards to accompany her!

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:08.080
Darling, calm down!

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:17.510
Cover for the Yamabuki Festival...

00:10:18.760 --> 00:10:21.390
And a big world debut...

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:22.760
Just kidding.

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:27.730
Jeez, what am I saying to myself?

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:34.070
But I'm really happy!

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:44.410
I was in the bath for too long. Now I feel dizzy.

00:10:45.920 --> 00:10:47.140
A text?

00:10:48.610 --> 00:10:50.880
Oh, it's from Arisawa-san!

00:10:51.230 --> 00:10:54.160
Hey! What's up, Yuno-san?

00:10:54.160 --> 00:10:58.300
Sorry for the short notice, but we have a group date tomorrow and we don't have enough people.

00:10:58.300 --> 00:10:59.920
I was wondering if you could come.

00:10:59.920 --> 00:11:01.390
What? Group da...

00:11:01.750 --> 00:11:03.720
Arisawa-san, long time no see.

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:07.650
Sorry, but I'm not very used to those kinds of things, so I don't think I can handle it.

00:11:07.650 --> 00:11:08.980
Sorry!

00:11:13.370 --> 00:11:15.070
I feel the same way!

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:18.060
Sorry, that was a joke.

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:25.650
Maybe this is good.

00:11:25.650 --> 00:11:26.620
Maybe it looks awkward.

00:11:28.270 --> 00:11:30.130
All right, I'm going with this!

00:11:33.130 --> 00:11:34.520
I'm off!

00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:36.630
See you!

00:11:36.760 --> 00:11:39.540
M-Miyako, where's Yuno going?!

00:11:39.540 --> 00:11:43.560
Don't tell me it's a d-d-d...

00:11:40.230 --> 00:11:43.560
You could just ask her yourself.

00:11:50.530 --> 00:11:51.640
<i>This looks great.</i>

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:53.820
<i>It has a mature feel.</i>

00:11:53.820 --> 00:11:57.780
<i>I wonder if I'll get to wear dresses like these when I go to college.</i>

00:12:00.350 --> 00:12:01.370
<i>Too much for me...</i>

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:07.660
<i>An art college student, huh?</i>

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:09.830
Yuno-san!

00:12:12.840 --> 00:12:14.480
Hey, what's up?

00:12:14.480 --> 00:12:15.590
Did I keep you waiting?

00:12:17.950 --> 00:12:19.800
Arisawa-san...

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:23.220
Hm? Why are you sighing like you're relieved?

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:28.540
Well, my image of an art college student
included a bazooka-like case and a panel bag.

00:12:28.540 --> 00:12:30.690
Even when they go out to eat with friends?

00:12:34.110 --> 00:12:35.400
We're here!

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:37.190
Let's get food here.

00:12:37.190 --> 00:12:38.880
This store looks so cute!

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:40.460
Do you come here often?

00:12:40.460 --> 00:12:42.570
Nah, it's my first time here.

00:12:42.910 --> 00:12:45.080
I wanted to check it out since
it seemed to have a nice atmosphere.

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:46.080
Welcome!

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:52.360
Yeah, the atmosphere in here is nice...

00:12:52.360 --> 00:12:54.420
...and of course that attracts these people.

00:12:58.170 --> 00:13:00.100
This looks delicious!

00:13:00.100 --> 00:13:00.760
Yeah!

00:13:00.930 --> 00:13:02.760
Let's eat!

00:13:07.270 --> 00:13:09.960
I will never be able to make something like this!

00:13:09.960 --> 00:13:12.240
Are you living alone now?

00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:13.650
Yup, since spring.

00:13:13.650 --> 00:13:16.780
But you look like you'd be a great cook, Arisawa-san.

00:13:16.780 --> 00:13:18.400
No, not at all.

00:13:18.710 --> 00:13:22.360
I have neither the skills nor the time, so it's always steamed rice with grilled fish.

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:23.520
Oh?

00:13:23.520 --> 00:13:28.780
But I never get tired of grilled salmon or mirin marinated and dried mackerel, you know?

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:29.660
Indeed.

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:33.330
<i>Arisawa-san is slowly turning into me.</i>

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:36.700
But that's not what I wanted to talk about.

00:13:36.700 --> 00:13:41.280
I invited you today to tell you about what I've been up to recently.

00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:44.220
Oh, I'd love to hear about your life in college!

00:13:44.220 --> 00:13:45.320
I'm sure you do!

00:13:45.320 --> 00:13:49.020
Back when I was a second-year, I wanted to hear about those kinds of things too.

00:13:51.480 --> 00:13:56.520
I thought school life wouldn't be so busy since you see college students working part-time and all,

00:13:56.520 --> 00:13:59.520
but there are a lot of assignments and things to do.

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:03.420
I'm not used to living by myself yet either.

00:14:03.420 --> 00:14:05.030
I'm always so busy!

00:14:06.270 --> 00:14:07.780
But it's fun!

00:14:07.780 --> 00:14:10.500
I have a lot of eccentric friends.

00:14:10.500 --> 00:14:15.080
Since I live near the campus, my friends drop by a lot for one reason or another.

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:16.460
It's so rowdy—

00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:19.460
Sorry, I guess you wanted to hear about how the classes are.

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:20.920
<i>That sounds so fun.</i>

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:24.060
Oh no, I'm curious about college life as a whole.

00:14:24.060 --> 00:14:26.180
Sorry. Thanks for being considerate.

00:14:27.430 --> 00:14:32.310
The practical class assignments are a lot more relevant to everyday life than I thought, so they're more interesting,

00:14:32.310 --> 00:14:37.220
especially after drawing all those submissions for entrance exams.

00:14:37.220 --> 00:14:38.690
Everyday life...

00:14:38.690 --> 00:14:42.600
So like designing a menu?

00:14:42.600 --> 00:14:43.280
Yeah!

00:14:45.660 --> 00:14:49.080
"Homemade apple pie hot from the brick oven."

00:14:49.080 --> 00:14:50.420
They recommend it.

00:14:50.420 --> 00:14:51.910
That sounds delicious!

00:14:54.920 --> 00:14:57.750
I get the feeling that you've become more mature, Yuno-san.

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:01.400
What? Have I?

00:15:01.400 --> 00:15:03.460
I don't feel anything myself.

00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:05.940
Pretty much the only thing I've changed is my shampoo.

00:15:05.940 --> 00:15:07.010
Your shampoo?

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:11.500
It smells like curry.

00:15:11.500 --> 00:15:14.680
Huh? That's not the scent of my shamp—

00:15:16.690 --> 00:15:20.940
Cleaning and recycling trash and all that is a big hassle when you're living alone, no?

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:24.860
It felt like a lot at first, but I got used to it.

00:15:24.860 --> 00:15:26.150
You're so mature.

00:15:26.670 --> 00:15:28.780
My wastebasket has a foot pedal.

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:31.410
It opens up when you step on it.

00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:34.620
Recently, I've taken to making it talk.

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:37.180
I step on the pedal to flip the lid and go,

00:15:37.180 --> 00:15:39.700
"Morning, it's a nice day today!"

00:15:39.700 --> 00:15:43.060
"Now what trash am I getting for breakfast?"

00:15:43.060 --> 00:15:43.920
like that.

00:15:46.410 --> 00:15:48.500
What? Is it that weird?

00:15:48.500 --> 00:15:50.840
It's not weird.

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:51.930
It's just funny.

00:15:52.750 --> 00:15:53.380
Is it?

00:15:53.380 --> 00:15:55.220
You should show me sometime.

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:57.200
I can't do that!

00:15:57.200 --> 00:15:58.560
It'd be too embarrassing.

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:01.540
Oh, but like that wastebasket,

00:16:01.540 --> 00:16:06.220
being able to choose things with the colors and shapes <i>you</i> want is one of the fun parts of living alone.

00:16:06.220 --> 00:16:07.580
I think so too!

00:16:07.580 --> 00:16:11.680
But I mostly brought things I already had at home.

00:16:11.680 --> 00:16:13.830
I didn't have much allowance left.

00:16:13.830 --> 00:16:15.140
I know what you mean.

00:16:15.140 --> 00:16:17.660
Fancy things are always expensive.

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:18.580
Yeah!

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:22.720
But the 100-yen shops nowadays are pretty amazing!

00:16:22.720 --> 00:16:25.040
They sell a lot of cute things for 100 yen,

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:28.270
so I bought a mountain of knick-knacks the other day!

00:16:28.270 --> 00:16:29.340
But...

00:16:30.250 --> 00:16:33.320
It's all stuff like a ceramic organizer, a small backboard,

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:37.040
and a cotton storage case with an iron button.

00:16:37.040 --> 00:16:39.020
I'll have to throw them out someday.

00:16:39.020 --> 00:16:41.320
I'm not sure which garbage bin I'll have to put them into.

00:16:41.320 --> 00:16:44.340
Thinking about that made me a little sad.

00:16:44.340 --> 00:16:47.070
<i>Today's conversation topic is garbage?</i>

00:16:47.450 --> 00:16:49.480
So, how's school?

00:16:49.480 --> 00:16:52.980
We just started getting ready for the Yamabuki Festival.

00:16:53.700 --> 00:16:57.290
Oh yeah, my art was chosen for the pamphlet cover!

00:16:57.290 --> 00:16:59.520
What? You won the competition?

00:16:59.520 --> 00:17:01.200
That's amazing, Yuno-san!

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:03.380
It's thanks to a friend's encouragement.

00:17:05.090 --> 00:17:06.960
You have a great friend.

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:09.090
It's important to keep in touch.

00:17:09.090 --> 00:17:10.720
Keep in touch?

00:17:10.720 --> 00:17:11.220
Yeah.

00:17:11.610 --> 00:17:14.560
We exchanged e-mail addresses,

00:17:14.560 --> 00:17:17.040
but it's been over six months since we last met face-to-face.

00:17:17.990 --> 00:17:22.300
I wasn't too worried, thinking I could get in touch with you anytime,

00:17:22.300 --> 00:17:26.230
but I realized you fall out of touch if you don't actually do so.

00:17:26.970 --> 00:17:29.720
It's hard to be aware of it when you're in an environment where it's easy to meet them,

00:17:29.720 --> 00:17:32.640
but to stay connected even after moving to a different environment,

00:17:32.640 --> 00:17:35.390
you need to take action, I guess.

00:17:35.390 --> 00:17:36.870
Arisawa-san...

00:17:38.050 --> 00:17:41.000
For people you want to keep in touch with.

00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:42.670
<i>What was that gunshot for?</i>

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:48.460
Time flew by! I have way more I want to talk about!

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:50.040
Please text me again sometime.

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:52.300
I'll try to keep in touch with you too.

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:53.760
Thank you.

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:57.240
Say, just call me Arisa from now on, okay?

00:17:57.240 --> 00:17:58.080
Arisa?

00:17:58.080 --> 00:18:00.320
Yeah, it's short for Arisawa.

00:18:00.320 --> 00:18:02.140
That's what everyone else calls me.

00:18:02.140 --> 00:18:03.460
Can I?

00:18:03.460 --> 00:18:04.900
Yeah, please do.

00:18:04.900 --> 00:18:07.440
Okay... Ari-san!

00:18:08.940 --> 00:18:09.460
Airy?

00:18:09.460 --> 00:18:10.580
S-Sorry!

00:18:10.580 --> 00:18:12.860
I was trying to say "Arisa-san."

00:18:14.450 --> 00:18:16.900
Yuno-san, you've always been like that.

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:21.040
And you just told me I became more mature too.

00:18:22.230 --> 00:18:24.290
You don't need to change.

00:18:24.730 --> 00:18:26.480
It's what makes you unique.

00:18:26.480 --> 00:18:28.090
What makes me unique...?

00:18:28.090 --> 00:18:29.430
Yep!

00:18:29.430 --> 00:18:32.090
For everyone, some things change, while some things stay the same.

00:18:32.630 --> 00:18:35.420
That's what makes people want to meet each other again.

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:42.320
All right, I'll be taking the bus home from here.

00:18:42.320 --> 00:18:43.820
Yuno-san, you're taking the train, right?

00:18:43.820 --> 00:18:44.560
Yes.

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:46.260
Good-bye, Yuno-san!

00:18:46.260 --> 00:18:47.700
Let's talk some more next time!

00:18:47.700 --> 00:18:48.380
Yeah! A...

00:18:48.380 --> 00:18:51.380
Arisa...wa-san.

00:18:51.380 --> 00:18:52.360
Arisa!

00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:54.450
Ari...sa-san!

00:18:54.450 --> 00:18:57.700
Would you come see the Yamabuki Festival?

00:18:57.700 --> 00:18:59.100
Thanks for the invitation.

00:18:59.100 --> 00:19:00.580
Of course I'll go!

00:19:02.580 --> 00:19:04.830
Yuno-san, keep it up!

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:06.940
You too, Arisa-san!

00:19:07.810 --> 00:19:09.340
See you later, then.

00:19:09.340 --> 00:19:10.420
Take care!

00:19:13.340 --> 00:19:16.640
<i>To stay connected even after moving to a different environment,</i>

00:19:16.640 --> 00:19:19.160
<i>you need to take action, I guess.</i>

00:19:19.730 --> 00:19:22.100
<i>If I put that another way...</i>

00:19:23.220 --> 00:19:26.350
<i>Even if I move to a different environment,</i>

00:19:26.350 --> 00:19:28.580
<i>I can stay in touch with others as long as I try.</i>

00:19:30.990 --> 00:19:31.680
I got a message.

00:19:31.680 --> 00:19:33.110
Oh, me too.

00:19:33.860 --> 00:19:35.540
<i>"Sae-san, Hiro-san!</i>

00:19:35.540 --> 00:19:38.240
<i>Let's be friends forever, okay?</i>

00:19:38.690 --> 00:19:41.060
<i>Oh, I have some apple pie with me.</i>

00:19:41.060 --> 00:19:43.040
<i>Would you like to come have some later?</i>

00:19:43.040 --> 00:19:44.000
<i>Yuno."</i>

00:19:45.500 --> 00:19:47.760
I wonder what happened.

00:19:47.760 --> 00:19:50.500
Let's ask when she's back.

00:19:54.010 --> 00:19:55.670
It's so hot!

00:19:55.670 --> 00:19:58.180
I love the scent of the apple!

00:19:58.180 --> 00:20:00.930
It's the same as the one I had at the shop!

00:20:00.930 --> 00:20:03.400
It's really good!

00:20:03.400 --> 00:20:05.240
Thank you, Yuno-san!

00:20:05.240 --> 00:20:07.270
So how was the date?

00:20:08.270 --> 00:20:10.060
Yuno-san, you were on a date?!

00:20:10.060 --> 00:20:11.270
With whom?!

00:20:11.270 --> 00:20:12.860
No, I wasn't.

00:20:12.860 --> 00:20:15.530
I was hanging out with Arisawa-san, an alumnus who went on to an art college.

00:20:15.530 --> 00:20:16.980
Were you invited?

00:20:16.980 --> 00:20:19.180
Or d-did you...

00:20:19.180 --> 00:20:20.700
What's Arisawa-san like?

00:20:21.250 --> 00:20:24.780
U-Um, I think you're misunderstanding.

00:20:24.780 --> 00:20:26.780
Arisawa-san is a girl.

00:20:26.780 --> 00:20:30.920
We just had lunch, followed by tea, then just talked.

00:20:30.920 --> 00:20:33.290
What?

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:36.350
Well, you were dressed up like it was a real date.

00:20:36.350 --> 00:20:38.220
It had been a while since I had last seen her.

00:20:38.220 --> 00:20:42.600
I would've gotten the wrong idea too, if Miyako didn't explain it to me.

00:20:42.600 --> 00:20:46.270
Arisawa-san has long hair and has an elegant air to her.

00:20:46.270 --> 00:20:49.020
But she's a fun, down-to-earth person.

00:20:49.350 --> 00:20:53.440
Today she talked a lot about mirin dried fish and garbage and stuff.

00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:56.000
While having lunch?!

00:20:56.000 --> 00:20:58.740
Oh, I guess that wasn't the best choice of topic.

00:20:59.490 --> 00:21:05.490
I was so glad we could talk like we used to before she graduated!

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:08.780
So that's where that came from.

00:21:11.130 --> 00:21:13.880
Yuno-san, thanks for the text today.

00:21:13.880 --> 00:21:15.240
You made me happy.

00:21:24.330 --> 00:21:26.840
I went downtown for a change to meet Arisawa.

00:21:26.840 --> 00:21:31.020
No, Arisa-san and I had a lot of fun chatting.

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:37.780
Yeah, to really stay in touch, I should send her a message too.

00:21:39.780 --> 00:21:42.120
But it's already kind of late now.

00:21:42.120 --> 00:21:43.660
Maybe I'll try tomorrow.

00:21:45.660 --> 00:21:46.660
No...

00:21:47.540 --> 00:21:50.740
Arisa-san, thank you for today.

00:21:50.740 --> 00:21:52.440
Let's hang out again.

00:21:52.440 --> 00:21:53.540
Good night!

00:21:53.540 --> 00:21:55.480
Send!

00:21:56.530 --> 00:21:57.300
Huh?

00:21:58.800 --> 00:22:01.140
<i>Yuno-san, today was a lot of fun!</i>

00:22:01.140 --> 00:22:02.640
<i>I look forward to seeing you again!</i>

00:22:02.640 --> 00:22:06.300
<i>Good night and sweet dreams!</i>

00:22:10.900 --> 00:22:12.950
We should host a cultural festival at Hidamari Apartments!

00:22:12.950 --> 00:22:14.270
We'll call it the Hidamari Festival!

00:22:14.270 --> 00:22:15.310
That could be fun.

00:22:15.310 --> 00:22:16.190
What would we do?

00:22:16.190 --> 00:22:18.170
Exhibitions and research poster sessions?

00:22:18.170 --> 00:22:19.970
I can't draw pictures.

00:22:19.970 --> 00:22:22.940
Research the lives of the residents of Hidamari Apartments!

00:22:22.940 --> 00:22:24.670
What about our privacy?

00:22:24.670 --> 00:22:26.250
Then, just censor everything.

00:22:26.250 --> 00:22:27.320
That's suspect.

00:22:27.320 --> 00:22:32.590
Next time: "October 11th and 30th, Terror! Preparing for the Yamabuki Festival."

00:22:32.590 --> 00:22:35.990
"November 3rd, Bizarre! The Day of the Yambuki Festival"

00:22:35.990 --> 00:22:39.210
We'll be waiting at Yamabuki High School, so come visit us!
